---
/**
 * C-1 · Contact orientation — `CONTACT_WIREFRAME.md` C-1 (Page IA Stage A).
 *
 * Responsibility realized: "confirm the visitor is in the right place to start a
 * conversation, calmly and without a sales opening."
 *
 * Components (Inventory), both of them and nothing else: "Section Header (page
 * intent) · Breadcrumb (parent context — orientation)."
 *
 * Spatial composition, transcribed: "a quiet, welcoming opening — a single clear
 * statement that this is where to begin, **no hero pitch, no re-explanation of
 * what the practice does**. The interface is calm and uncluttered; the tone is
 * *'let's talk,'* not *'let me convince you.'*"
 *
 * ── THE BREADCRUMB IS ONE LEVEL, BECAUSE CONTACT IS ────────────────────────
 * Contact is a standalone top-level page (IA Step 7, "Type: Standalone"), so its
 * parent context is the Homepage and nothing else. The Work Entry's three-level
 * crumb (archive → pillar → entry) has no equivalent here, and inventing an
 * intermediate level would assert a hierarchy the IA does not have. Marked up as
 * an ordered list inside a labelled `<nav>` — the same structure `Hero.astro`
 * uses, so the two pages announce their crumbs identically.
 *
 * No coordinate rail and no section marker: both are instruments of the paced,
 * multi-station page types (HP, HUB, RC, WE, SV), and Contact is a single
 * uninterrupted act. `WorkArchive.astro` records the same reasoning for its own
 * missing rail.
 *
 * ── TWO COMPOSITION MOVES, NEITHER OF THEM NEW CONTENT ─────────────────────
 *  1. **The breadcrumb and the eyebrow share one baseline.** Both are 11px mono
 *     roles, and the section marker used by every paced page type already puts a
 *     label at the inline start and a running coordinate at the inline end of one
 *     rule (`SectionMarker.astro`). This is that geometry, applied to the two
 *     11px roles Contact actually has. DOM order is unchanged — nav, then the
 *     eyebrow that labels the heading below it.
 *  2. **The statement is rendered by `ContactPage.astro`, not here.** It is still
 *     C-1 content and still reads immediately after the heading; it is composed
 *     into the lead block beside the form so that the desktop canvas carries
 *     weight on both sides instead of one. See the composition note in
 *     `ContactPage.astro` and the grid in `styles/pages/contact.css`.
 */
import type { Locale } from '../../lib/content';
import type { ContactMessages } from '../../lib/i18n/contact';
import { routePath } from '../../lib/i18n/routes';

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
  copy: ContactMessages['orientation'];
}

const { locale, copy } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="c-intro" aria-labelledby="c-heading">
  <div class="c-intro-top">
    <nav class="c-crumbs-nav" aria-label={copy.breadcrumbLabel}>
      <ol class="c-crumbs">
        <li><a href={routePath('home', locale)}>{copy.home}</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">{copy.here}</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <p class="eyebrow rv" data-rv="meta">{copy.eyebrow}</p>
  </div>

  <h1 class="c-title rv" data-rv="head" id="c-heading">{copy.heading}</h1>
</section>
